there is in line 1286, it\'s using the dollar sign, uh, uh, bang important, which basically says in CSS, you want to override what the parent one is. Um, but what it\'s actually typing in there, Ed, if you go in inspect element on the page, what color does it actually say? because the color on there will um in the styles section over there instead of computed you can inspect element and then click on the thing and you\'ll see um the the code will actually tell you which class that color is actually coming from and actually yes I\'m not going to go into detail on this just because this is not supposed to be this class but this is a class we need to do because when you start debugging what so What I did here is I\'ve now changed to opus and opus failed. Okay, so um and a lot of times with uh vibe coding you need to pick your battles like at a certain point you just decide, hey, is this really worth changing to red? Because I could do a lot of other things like I could go into courses here. I could go into available courses and I could say in any every place it is remove these um these badges. I mean this whole thing like this canband board that I can do drag and drops on where it says task move it successfully all of that was written by this code. Now as the project gets more and more complicated the AI has to do more and more work to be able to do it. But you notice that the the combination of the LLM and the tools lets it do a lot of other things. So, let me go here to the dashboard. I\'m going to go, what do I want to do here? I got team members. Oh, this is actually a funny one. One thing that I was fighting with today is I actually have a profile picture. So, if I go up here to profile, I uploaded a random picture, but in the team members display, it\'s not showing the picture. So, at a certain point here, you do have to pick your battles because I actually spent a good amount of time on this today trying to figure out why the profile picture wasn\'t actually printing. So, um All right. So, couple other things that I wanted to cover is go ahead. Right there. um in your styles there you see the dot welcome banner and dot alert heading is still showing color white important and it\'s also telling you that that is in custom.css CSS on line 1045. So if you click on it, you can see exactly where that is. And if you wanted to, you could then go into the CSS and not Vibe Code and actually go through and change that to red in that file, right? Although but that\'s only if you have it open in like uh an IDE like cursor or whatever. Um and that\'s that\'s that\'s not background color. That\'s that color. color is equal to text color again in in font but there is no BG color there. Okay, I see that. Okay, so but these are these are the types of things that so vibe coding is gives you superpowers. Oh, I just changed I changed this to blue. Uh vibe coding gives you superpowers. But the reason that you want to do the courses and you want to work with this is to just start to get the skills and start figuring out how you debug things and how you write the requirements. And there\'s a lot to this. So in the and I think in our next beginners course I\'m going to cover um setting up your environment and then just starting a project from scratch because I want to get people especially in the pro community. I want to get people started working on some projects. Uh because that\'s just really going to be the fastest way to learn is uh you know I\'ve learned I\'ve learned clawed code the most by fighting with it. You know trying to make it do things and then seeing all the things it can\'t do. And uh there\'s I\'ve made a lot of changes to the way I go about doing projects because I\'ve tried to do projects. Now, if you are one of the people who\'s who\'s learning divide code and you\'re learning AI because you want to develop and sell products, the LAMP stack, which is this Linux, Apache, MySQL, and PHP, is one of the most accepted stacks if you\'re going to sell software into an enterprise because all the code is readable and you can do design reviews on it. If you\'re coding in a compiled language like Angular or React, it is very hard to get code approved by the security department because it\'s compiled code. It\'s very difficult to read and it\'s, you know, there could always be Trojans or things in the background. So, you do get a lot of benefits by programming in the older programming languages. So, that\'s just one thing I want to keep uh pointing out. So, all right, the hour is up. Thank you all for attending. Um, we I will I will try to get this thing rendered and pushed up tonight. Um, if not, it\'ll be first thing in the morning. Uh, but uh I\'m guessing this went half through your slides, Ed, or did you get through all your slides? No, I actually got through all my slides because I didn\'t take questions like I did on the weekend. So, there because I could that that\'s how that would work. So yes, I will make more slides for next time, but this turned out to be exactly an hour. So all right everybody, I\'ll give you your evening or day or whatever time of the day it is back and uh I look forward to seeing you all again and see you online. Um uh please post any kind of questions on this in the school community. Um, you will most likely get an answer from someone else in the community before we get to them all, but I know that there was a bunch during the um the actual presentation, but we\'re not taking the doing the questions today. Yeah. But we will set up a followup live where all we do is take questions and uh if you want to post in the community when you think a good time with for that would be I did get a lot of I definitely got a lot of feedback on this time but we\'ve kind of been neglecting our Australian friends for the ones we\'ve been doing in the mornings because it\'s been like 3 in the morning for all of the stuff we\'ve been doing. So, um maybe we\'ll set up lives in different time zones so we can uh you know answer the questions. Um Joe, do we have a way to uh to say to log the chat? Um I do not know that before. Well, you can drop it and Oh, there\'s a there\'s a save chat button here. Um save chat. Show and finder. Okay. So, I have the meeting save chat. Yes, I do. Beautiful. All right. So, we\'ll just go through and we\'ll start answering some of these in the in the in the community.');
