(65, 31, 'Introduction to Hugging Face - Ed', 'This is a quick introduction to hugging face.', '', 'text', 6, 5, 'published', 1, 'https://youtu.be/buaT9etYFf0', 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, '2025-07-28 23:29:21', '2025-07-28 23:29:22', NULL, 'okay so in this section I want to talk about cloud accounts these are the accounts that you\'re going to uh sign up for and you\'re going to need and the first one that you\'re going to need is something called hugging face think of hugging face as the GitHub of of artificial intelligence it\'s where you go to get models it\'s where you go to you can run things on hugging face so it\'s a lot like Google Collab in that you can you know if you want to try things out hugging face is a is a great place to do it so let me jump over uh to my Google Chrome and go to my hugging face so here is hugging face now hugging face you sign up uh it it is free there is a paid version of it i do the paid version and I\'m I don\'t remember what it was but there was something about it that made it worth it for me to pay $20 i think it has to do with the speed at which you download these models i think they\'re very very throttled if you\'re downloading from hugging face and you\'re not paying so yeah I think that was pretty much it when you\'re when you\'re downloading you know a 30 gigabyte file or a 50 gigabyte file you do not want your download speed to be throttled because you you find yourself sitting there for 15 minutes so in this case I\'ve got you know you\'ve got your models it it looks incredibly like GitHub so it\'s also a lot like a social media platform and that you can message each other you can follow each other you can follow each other\'s repositories so if you\'re here you can come here and this is everything so you can go and you can get models okay so these are all models that I\'ve uploaded and then you can go search for other people\'s models data sets i don\'t have any of my own data sets so let me come up to here so models these are all the models that you\'re going to find so a lot of the latest models you can check to see which are the most um used models um which are the most downloaded and you know just um follow you basically you can follow a lot of different models that a lot of different people have done supervised fine training on now if you\'re going to be doing supervised fine-tuning yourself or you\'re going to be you know training models uh data sets is where you can come and download a bunch of different data sets you know people post their data sets you can also post your data sets up here so that you can know you know so that you can just um create data maybe you\'re creating synthetic data but this is a place where you share a lot like GitHub so data sets are something you know you can actually go into any of these data sets and you can see uh there\'s a data set viewer there\'s a data set card that tells you what\'s actually in this data set this the size of this data set is 142 megabytes So you know you\'ve you\'ve got your choice for your data sets and then you have spaces now hugging face spaces is a really interesting concept it\'s really where you can create models with hugging uh hugging phase and then create an environment that people can test out your models so I can So this guy over here he has an image to 3D generation space so it\'s got 332 likes so I\'m going to go into that and you actually have the ability to use his model so I\'m going to I don\'t actually know anything about this so uh gen generate a shape okay i\'m not actually sure how to do this so I\'m not going to go too deep into it but so spaces is another thing that is actually really uh you know valuable for you if you\'re going to uh train models and or you\'re going to develop apps and then you want to show them off to the world now keep in mind this community if you\'re showing them off to the world in hugging face these are not potential clients these are other developers like you um now we also have docs okay and inside of here there are there is training there\'s actually really good training inside of Hugging Face i think it\'s called HuggingFace Learn and I will actually uh find that link and make sure I have it posted you know as a good place for you to go to and get information so you\'ve got your docs you got your enterprise and I\'ll come over here to pricing so the pro account is basically really you know it gives you opportunity to uh do good things i I\'m actually I\'m not actually 100% sure the difference between pro and teams i know I\'m paying for teams so I\'m not actually sure uh what the difference between pro and teams is so yeah so this is hugging face so this is going to be the first thing that you\'re going to want to sign up for okay so um the other thing here is in very often you\'re going to need hugging face access tokens so if I come over here to access tokens I can log back in confirm my identity and you\'re actually creating access tokens that you can use in things like Google Collab you can um use it in your when you\'re doing fine-tuning you can use it basically if you need to access anything programmatically from Hugging Face you\'re going to need an access token whether you pay for Hugging Face or you don\'t pay for Hugging Face doesn\'t really matter in either way you\'re going to need an access token for it so this is your place you\'re coming for your models your data your data sets you can run things here there\'s just a lot you can do with HuggingFace which is why you need to include it in your uh AI ecosystem it just needs to be something that you have one of no matter how much you use it you know you just need you know it\'s like a GitHub account you need to make sure that you have one'),
(66, 31, 'Ed\'s Introduction to Google Colab', 'This is my brief introduction to Google Colab', '', 'text', 3, 1, 'published', 1, 'https://youtu.be/7jGcwVc-jJY', 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, '2025-07-28 23:31:52', '2025-07-28 23:32:14', NULL, 'okay the next thing I want to talk about is Google Collab so Google Collab is it\'s built on Jupyter Notebooks which is a way for you to run Python code step by step so it is the best possible Jupyter Notebooks is the best possible way to learn Python but it\'s also a great way to be able to do things for like supervised fine-tuning if you don\'t have the GPUs you need either on your desktop or on your MacBook uh or well actually if you have a MacBook be you can\'t run Unsloth because you don\'t have an Nvidia GPU card so Google Collab is the easiest way to get a Python development environment that\'s has GPUs available for you so let me go over to Google Collab and so it is at it\'s at collab.resarch.google.com i\'m sure I\'m already uh logged in so inside of Google Collab you work with something called Jupyter Notebooks and Jupyter Notebooks is a way for you to Let me just open one of my notebooks uh this one\'s called PDF to JSON tool so as you see that we the code is actually broken up into steps so this is just a way for you to this is a notebook and so I can actually learn Python by going step by step through other people\'s code and if I want to do supervised fine-tuning I\'ve got access to GPUs over here i\'ve got access to my keys and then up here at my runtime I can actually change my runtime type to so I\'m running Python 3 I can say I want an A100 GPU because I\'m actually paying for Collab so I could run on an A100 and so that if I\'m doing some supervised fine-tuning and I need a GPU for whatever I\'m doing this is a good way for you to be able to uh learn Python and test out different um different GPU configurations and you know this is just a really actually just a really good way to learn so it\'s and a lot of the training that I do when I\'m teaching Python it\'s going to be done in Google Collab so for instance so I in this case I I\'m writing some code that does named entity recognition which means it\'s going to go into a PDF file turn it into text send the text to the large language model and then pull back um pull back different uh extract different data from the PDF so in this case prototyping this project was best done in Google Collab because I could go section by section test each section look at the varial variables make sure everything works and then go on to the next section so uh Google Collab is another thing that you just want to have as part of your cloud tools in your AI ecosystem'),
(67, 31, 'Introduction to Gitub - Beginners', 'Although Git is not an AI tool, it is vital for almost everything you do with projects using AI', '', 'text', 23, 9, 'published', 1, 'https://youtu.be/Oaj3RBIoGFc', 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, '2025-07-28 23:35:00', '2025-07-28 23:35:00', NULL, 'Automatic transcript retrieval requires OAuth authentication. Please use OAuth flow or manually add transcript. Video title: GitHub Basics Made Easy: A Fast Beginner\'s Tutorial!'),
