ng you code in Typescript. So, um, the whole concept of being able to pull things in and pull things out as you need them at the different steps of the process, that that\'s going to be an important skill to have that I need to do a little research on it to get better at it myself because I\'ve noticed that when I\'m coding that if I if I change topics right away and don\'t clear out the context, you know, if I\'m I\'m doing a bunch of database stuff, then I start saying, \"Hey, move these buttons around.\" and it\'s going from database stuff with MySQL to bootstrap 5 uh class libraries, then that\'s so far apart from each other. What I should be doing in that case is exiting out of claude, going back into claude. So none of that is actually in the uh in the context. Do you have do you have a a tip for data structure uh for giving the the perfect context because you just said like there is like noise and if you don\'t want to provide like most of the people they will just throw the thing like uh like that and yeah uh deal with it uh I think it\'s it\'s the best like to filter and structure it and limit to some uh context. I\'m not sure how do you do that? Yeah. So MD files the the markdown format that you see um and actually ask you know you can that\'s something you can even ask Claude or Chad even Chad GPT gets it right. So you want that you want to put it into the context in markdown formats because that\'s a hierarchical structure of this and then these are dependent on that and it it kind of tells the LLM all the relationships between the things in the file. So it does it\'s got a lot less work. it has to do to ingest it. So, um yeah, MD files are the the the the markdown format is the the format that you would want to use. Yeah. If if you have like a tip like of uh how to I mean uh limit uh the the the [Music] search like uh of uh of the context like to to put some let\'s say limits. Yes. and and um I\'m not sure if uh if um how do you let\'s say if you have d