erts was an innovative way to not have the models use all of the parameters. It\'s more like showing up at a college campus and the first place you go to is the reception desk who tells you what buildings you need to go to. So with the mixture of experts models, which mixtrol is one of those, it is going to use it. It takes the entire model and it breaks it up into call it departments. So it\'s like I\'m going to ask a question. It\'s going to go to something like a router and that router is going to say, \"Oh, you need chemistry and physics, go that way.\" Oh, you need uh uh human studies and something else, go that way. Now, what mixture of experts always does is it recommends two areas to go into so that they can fact check each other. Now, what makes Mixtixure of Experts models so powerful is they run much more efficiently and with much less power. So, when you\'re getting to models that have let\'s say 5 trillion parameters in them, a mixture of experts model is going to use far less electricity and you\'re going to be able to run it on far less hardware than you would if you\'re running a dense model. Because a dense model, the entire LLM has to fit into into GPU memory for you to run it. Whereas with a mixture of experts model, it\'s going to come back slower, but it\'s going to load the sections into the GPU as it needs it. Now, the second thing I have on this list are the thinking models or the reasoning models. and chat GPT40 came out to be the first and then Deep Seek came out and kind of said, \"Hey, we\'re here and you\'re you\'re we\'re here to stay.\" The thinking models are really taking over because the biggest thing about them is they eliminate hallucinations by attacking a problem from multiple steps and actually thinking through the reasoning of the answer. Now chat GPT03 is one of is their big reasoning model and then this the claude uh claude for opus is their big thinking model and the thinking models are incredibly powerful but they\'re also 