al that you want to put in with the user input. But let\'s say I created my own chatbot. And in my own chatbot, I wanted to answer medical questions. And so in addition to the users\'s input, what they\'re putting in, I want to add some more things as part of the system prompt. I want to add that persona. I want to say, uh, you are a helpful physician\'s assistant. So, I\'m adding things in the pre-processing as part of developing the tool where I\'m pre-processing the uh users\'s input and then I\'m injecting other context. So, maybe let\'s say we\'re asking questions about longevity and we\'re asking questions about a specific longevity paper. Well, we inject that paper into the context so that the LLM has it to work with. So, we have our user input, we have our pre-processing, and then we have our prompting. So, we\'re actually now going back getting more a prompt out of the user input and the pre uh processing. That\'s a prompt that\'s sent to the model. We get the model\'s response and then we do post-processing. So in some cases we\'re going to take what comes out of the model. Maybe we ask the model to give us a JSON object and we want to take that and we want to reform format that into another maybe it\'s bullet points or maybe it\'s a different kind of object or maybe we want to put it in a database. So that\'s your post-processing and then you have your feedback and your iteration. So that\'s your typical workflow of a prompting either when the prompting is automated or you\'re doing it at the chat window. Now a critical part critical thing that is really not part oops not part of prompt engineering but really is is retrieval augmented generation. Now retrieval augmented generation is an art form and it is basically gathering data that\'s going into the prompt. So when we\'re here and we\'re at our pre-processing and contacts injection, this is where retrieval augmented generation goes. And in retrieval augmented generation, we\'re taking that prompt that 