INSERT INTO `project_requirements` (`id`, `project_id`, `category_id`, `title`, `description`, `priority`, `status`, `created_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(2, 46, 10, 'ContentGaps AI - Product Requirements Doc', '# ContentGaps AI - Product Requirements Document\r\n\r\n## Executive Summary\r\n**Product**: ContentGaps AI - Content Strategy Intelligence Platform  \r\n**Timeline**: 5-7 days development + 2 days testing/launch  \r\n**Target Price**: $79-199/month  \r\n**Core Value**: Identify content opportunities your competitors have covered but you haven\'t\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Product Overview\r\n\r\n### Problem Statement\r\nContent teams struggle to:\r\n- Identify trending topics before competitors discover them\r\n- Understand what content gaps exist in their strategy\r\n- Find content opportunities that drive actual traffic and engagement\r\n- Stay ahead of industry conversations and developments\r\n\r\n### Solution\r\nAn AI-powered platform that analyzes competitor content, identifies trending topics, and surfaces content opportunities using real-time web intelligence via Perplexity Search API.\r\n\r\n### Target Users\r\n- **Primary**: Content marketing managers (companies with 50-500 employees)\r\n- **Secondary**: SEO agencies, freelance content strategists, B2B marketing teams\r\n- **Tertiary**: Publishers and media companies\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Core Features (MVP)\r\n\r\n### 1. Competitor Content Analysis Engine\r\n**User Story**: \"As a content manager, I want to see what content topics my competitors have covered that I haven\'t, so I can identify gaps in my content strategy.\"\r\n\r\n**Technical Implementation**:\r\n```python\r\n# Core analysis flow\r\ndef analyze_competitor_content_gaps(user_domain, competitor_domains, timeframe):\r\n    # Step 1: Extract competitor recent content\r\n    competitor_content = []\r\n    for domain in competitor_domains:\r\n        content = perplexity_search(\r\n            query=f\"site:{domain} recent articles blogs {timeframe}\",\r\n            filters={\r\n                \"domains\": [domain],\r\n                \"time_range\": timeframe,\r\n                \"content_type\": [\"article\", \"blog\", \"news\"]\r\n            }\r\n        )\r\n        competitor_content.extend(content)\r\n    \r\n    # Step 2: Extract topics and themes\r\n    topics = extract_topics_ai(competitor_content)\r\n    \r\n    # Step 3: Check user\'s content coverage\r\n    user_content_coverage = check_content_coverage(user_domain, topics)\r\n    \r\n    # Step 4: Identify gaps and opportunities\r\n    content_gaps = identify_gaps(topics, user_content_coverage)\r\n    \r\n    return rank_opportunities(content_gaps)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**UI Components**:\r\n- Competitor domain input (up to 5 competitors for MVP)\r\n- Time range selector (last 7, 30, 90 days)\r\n- Content gap visualization (topic clusters)\r\n- Opportunity scoring dashboard\r\n- Export functionality (CSV, PDF report)\r\n\r\n### 2. Trending Topic Discovery\r\n**User Story**: \"As a content strategist, I want to identify emerging topics in my industry before they become oversaturated, so I can create first-mover content.\"\r\n\r\n**Technical Implementation**:\r\n```python\r\ndef discover_trending_topics(industry_keywords, geographic_scope=\"global\"):\r\n    # Step 1: Industry trend detection\r\n    trending_content = perplexity_search(\r\n        query=f\"{\' OR \'.join(industry_keywords)} trending news analysis\",\r\n        filters={\r\n            \"time_range\": \"last_24_hours\",\r\n            \"geographic_scope\": geographic_scope,\r\n            \"domains\": [\"authoritative_domains\"]  # Pre-curated list\r\n        }\r\n    )\r\n    \r\n    # Step 2: Trend velocity calculation\r\n    trend_scores = calculate_trend_velocity(trending_content)\r\n    \r\n    # Step 3: Competitive saturation analysis\r\n    saturation_scores = analyze_competitive_saturation(trending_content)\r\n    \r\n    # Step 4: Opportunity ranking\r\n    opportunities = rank_trending_opportunities(trend_scores, saturation_scores)\r\n    \r\n    return opportunities\r\n```\r\n\r\n**UI Components**:\r\n- Industry keyword setup (saved profiles)\r\n- Geographic targeting options\r\n- Trend velocity indicators\r\n- Competitive saturation heatmap\r\n- Topic alerting system\r\n\r\n### 3. Content Opportunity Scoring\r\n**User Story**: \"As a marketing manager, I want to prioritize content opportunities based on potential impact, so I can allocate resources effectively.\"\r\n\r\n**Scoring Algorithm**:\r\n```python\r\ndef calculate_opportunity_score(topic_data):\r\n    factors = {\r\n        \"search_volume\": get_search_trend_data(topic_data.keywords),\r\n        \"competitive_difficulty\": analyze_serp_competition(topic_data.keywords),\r\n        \"trend_velocity\": calculate_momentum(topic_data.mentions_over_time),\r\n        \"brand_relevance\": calculate_brand_fit(topic_data.content, user_brand_profile),\r\n        \"content_freshness\": assess_content_recency(topic_data.recent_coverage),\r\n        \"social_signals\": analyze_social_engagement(topic_data.social_mentions)\r\n    }\r\n    \r\n    # Weighted scoring model\r\n    score = (\r\n        factors[\"search_volume\"] * 0.25 +\r\n        factors[\"competitive_difficulty\"] * 0.20 +  # Lower is better\r\n        factors[\"trend_velocity\"] * 0.20 +\r\n        factors[\"brand_relevance\"] * 0.15 +\r\n        factors[\"content_freshness\"] * 0.10 +\r\n        factors[\"social_signals\"] * 0.10\r\n    )\r\n    \r\n    return min(100, max(0, score))  # Normalize to 0-100\r\n```\r\n\r\n**UI Components**:\r\n- Opportunity score dashboard (0-100 scale)\r\n- Factor breakdown visualization\r\n- Filtering by score ranges\r\n- Bulk actions for high-scoring opportunities\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Technical Architecture\r\n\r\n### Backend Stack (Recommended for Speed)\r\n```python\r\n# FastAPI + SQLite for rapid development\r\n# main.py\r\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, BackgroundTasks\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine\r\nfrom perplexity import Perplexity\r\nimport asyncio\r\n\r\napp = FastAPI()\r\nperplexity_client = Perplexity()\r\n\r\n# Database Models\r\nclass ContentGap(Base):\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    user_id = Column(String)\r\n    topic = Column(String)\r\n    competitors_covered = Column(JSON)\r\n    opportunity_score = Column(Float)\r\n    created_at = Column(DateTime)\r\n\r\nclass TrendingTopic(Base):\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    topic = Column(String)\r\n    trend_velocity = Column(Float)\r\n    competitive_saturation = Column(Float)\r\n    geographic_scope = Column(String)\r\n    detected_at = Column(DateTime)\r\n\r\n# Core API Endpoints\r\n@app.post(\"/api/analyze-gaps\")\r\nasync def analyze_content_gaps(request: ContentGapRequest):\r\n    # Async analysis using background tasks\r\n    task_id = generate_task_id()\r\n    background_tasks.add_task(run_content_gap_analysis, request, task_id)\r\n    return {\"task_id\": task_id, \"status\": \"processing\"}\r\n\r\n@app.get(\"/api/trending-topics\")\r\nasync def get_trending_topics(industry: str, geo: str = \"global\"):\r\n    # Real-time trending topic discovery\r\n    topics = await discover_trending_topics(industry, geo)\r\n    return {\"topics\": topics, \"updated_at\": datetime.now()}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Frontend Stack (Recommended for Speed)\r\n```javascript\r\n// Next.js + Tailwind + Recharts for rapid development\r\n// components/ContentGapDashboard.jsx\r\nimport { useState, useEffect } from \'react\'\r\nimport { BarChart, Bar, XAxis, YAxis, ResponsiveContainer } from \'recharts\'\r\n\r\nexport function ContentGapDashboard({ userDomain }) {\r\n    const [contentGaps, setContentGaps] = useState([])\r\n    const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false)\r\n    const [competitors, setCompetitors] = useState([\'\'])\r\n    \r\n    const analyzeGaps = async () => {\r\n        setLoading(true)\r\n        try {\r\n            const response = await fetch(\'/api/analyze-gaps\', {\r\n                method: \'POST\',\r\n                headers: { \'Content-Type\': \'application/json\' },\r\n                body: JSON.stringify({\r\n                    userDomain,\r\n                    competitors: competitors.filter(c => c.trim()),\r\n                    timeframe: \'30_days\'\r\n                })\r\n            })\r\n            const result = await response.json()\r\n            // Poll for results\r\n            pollForResults(result.task_id)\r\n        } catch (error) {\r\n            console.error(\'Analysis failed:\', error)\r\n        } finally {\r\n            setLoading(false)\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n    \r\n    return (\r\n        <div className=\"space-y-6\">\r\n            <CompetitorInput \r\n                competitors={competitors}\r\n                setCompetitors={setCompetitors}\r\n                onAnalyze={analyzeGaps}\r\n                loading={loading}\r\n            />\r\n            <ContentGapVisualization gaps={contentGaps} />\r\n            <OpportunityScoreTable gaps={contentGaps} />\r\n        </div>\r\n    )\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Data Flow Architecture\r\n```\r\nUser Input → API Gateway → Perplexity Search API → Content Processing →\r\nTopic Extraction → Gap Analysis → Opportunity Scoring → Results Cache →\r\nFrontend Dashboard → Export/Alerts\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## User Experience Flow\r\n\r\n### 1. Onboarding (First Use)\r\n1. User enters their domain/website\r\n2. Adds 3-5 competitor domains\r\n3. Selects industry keywords (with suggested list)\r\n4. Chooses analysis frequency (weekly/daily)\r\n5. Runs first analysis (takes 2-3 minutes)\r\n\r\n### 2. Daily Workflow\r\n1. User logs in to dashboard\r\n2. Reviews new content gaps (highlighted)\r\n3. Explores trending topics in their industry\r\n4. Prioritizes opportunities by score\r\n5. Exports content brief for team\r\n6. Sets up alerts for specific topics\r\n\r\n### 3. Reporting & Export\r\n- **Content Gap Report**: PDF with competitor analysis and recommendations\r\n- **Opportunity Brief**: Formatted content briefs ready for writers\r\n- **Trend Alert**: Daily/weekly email with emerging topics\r\n- **API Access**: JSON endpoints for integration with existing tools\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Monetization Strategy\r\n\r\n### Pricing Tiers\r\n1. **Starter** ($79/month):\r\n   - 3 competitor analysis\r\n   - Weekly gap analysis\r\n   - 50 trending topics/month\r\n   - Basic reporting\r\n\r\n2. **Professional** ($149/month):\r\n   - 10 competitor analysis\r\n   - Daily gap analysis\r\n   - 200 trending topics/month\r\n   - Advanced scoring\r\n   - Priority support\r\n\r\n3. **Agency** ($199/month):\r\n   - Unlimited competitors\r\n   - Real-time analysis\r\n   - Unlimited trending topics\r\n   - White-label reports\r\n   - API access\r\n\r\n### Revenue Projections (Conservative)\r\n- Month 1-2: 50 users × $79 = $3,950/month\r\n- Month 3-6: 200 users × $120 avg = $24,000/month\r\n- Month 6-12: 500 users × $135 avg = $67,500/month\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Development Timeline: 7 Days\r\n\r\n### Day 1-2: Core Infrastructure\r\n- [ ] Set up FastAPI backend with SQLite\r\n- [ ] Implement Perplexity Search API integration\r\n- [ ] Create basic database models\r\n- [ ] Build content analysis pipeline\r\n\r\n### Day 3-4: Frontend Development\r\n- [ ] Next.js app with authentication\r\n- [ ] Competitor input interface\r\n- [ ] Content gap visualization dashboard\r\n- [ ] Trending topics page\r\n\r\n### Day 5-6: Analysis Engine\r\n- [ ] Topic extraction and clustering\r\n- [ ] Opportunity scoring algorithm\r\n- [ ] Competitive analysis logic\r\n- [ ] Export functionality\r\n\r\n### Day 7: Polish & Launch Prep\r\n- [ ] Responsive design cleanup\r\n- [ ] Error handling and validation\r\n- [ ] Performance optimization\r\n- [ ] Deploy to production\r\n\r\n### Tools Strategy for 7-Day Development\r\n1. **Claude Code**: Architecture decisions, complex algorithms, API integrations\r\n2. **Cursor**: Frontend components, UI logic, styling\r\n3. **VS Code**: Database operations, utility functions, debugging\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Success Metrics\r\n\r\n### Technical KPIs\r\n- Analysis completion time < 3 minutes\r\n- Topic extraction accuracy > 85%\r\n- System uptime > 99%\r\n- API response time < 2 seconds\r\n\r\n### Business KPIs  \r\n- User activation rate > 40% (complete first analysis)\r\n- Monthly retention > 70%\r\n- Net Promoter Score > 50\r\n- Average revenue per user > $120\r\n\r\n### Product-Market Fit Indicators\r\n- Users run analysis at least 2x/month\r\n- 60%+ of users upgrade from free trial\r\n- Organic referral rate > 15%\r\n- Feature request volume indicates strong engagement\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Risk Mitigation\r\n\r\n### Technical Risks\r\n- **Perplexity API Rate Limits**: Implement intelligent caching and batching\r\n- **Content Analysis Accuracy**: Use multiple validation methods and user feedback\r\n- **Scalability**: Start with SQLite, plan PostgreSQL migration path\r\n\r\n### Market Risks  \r\n- **Competition**: Focus on speed-to-market and superior UX\r\n- **Pricing Sensitivity**: Offer freemium tier with limited features\r\n- **Customer Acquisition**: Leverage existing MentionIQ user base\r\n\r\n### Operational Risks\r\n- **Support Burden**: Build comprehensive self-service resources\r\n- **Content Quality**: Implement user feedback loops for continuous improvement\r\n- **Compliance**: Ensure proper web scraping ethics and respect robots.txt\r\n\r\nThis PRD provides a clear roadmap for building ContentGaps AI in 7 days while establishing a strong foundation for scaling and iterating based on user feedback.', 'must_have', 'pending', 70, '2025-09-26 01:53:37', '2025-09-26 01:53:37'),
(3, 47, 10, 'LocalIQ Monitor - Product Requirements Doc (V.1)', '# LocalIQ Monitor - Product Requirements Document\r\n\r\n## Executive Summary\r\n**Product**: LocalIQ Monitor - Geographic SEO Intelligence Platform  \r\n**Timeline**: 4-5 days development + 1 day testing/launch  \r\n**Target Price**: $49-149/month per location  \r\n**Core Value**: Monitor brand mentions, competitor activity, and local search performance across specific geographic markets\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Product Overview\r\n\r\n### Problem Statement\r\nLocal and multi-location businesses struggle with:\r\n- Tracking brand mentions in specific geographic markets\r\n- Understanding local competitor activities and mentions\r\n- Monitoring local search performance across multiple locations\r\n- Managing reputation across different cities/regions\r\n- Identifying local content and PR opportunities\r\n\r\n### Solution\r\nA location-based brand intelligence platform that uses Perplexity\'s geographic filtering to monitor mentions, competitor activities, and search performance for specific cities, regions, or market areas.\r\n\r\n### Target Users\r\n- **Primary**: Multi-location businesses (retail chains, restaurants, service franchises)\r\n- **Secondary**: Local SEO agencies managing clients across different markets\r\n- **Tertiary**: Real estate companies, healthcare networks, financial services\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Core Features (MVP)\r\n\r\n### 1. Geographic Brand Monitoring\r\n**User Story**: \"As a franchise owner, I want to monitor brand mentions specifically in my market area, so I can respond to local issues and opportunities quickly.\"\r\n\r\n**Technical Implementation**:\r\n```python\r\nclass GeographicBrandMonitor:\r\n    def __init__(self, perplexity_client):\r\n        self.perplexity = perplexity_client\r\n    \r\n    async def monitor_brand_by_location(self, brand_name, locations):\r\n        \"\"\"Monitor brand mentions across specific geographic locations\"\"\"\r\n        location_data = {}\r\n        \r\n        for location in locations:\r\n            geo_query = self.build_geographic_query(brand_name, location)\r\n            \r\n            # Use Perplexity\'s geographic filtering\r\n            mentions = await self.perplexity.search(\r\n                query=geo_query,\r\n                filters={\r\n                    \"geographic_scope\": location[\'geo_filter\'],\r\n                    \"time_range\": \"last_7_days\",\r\n                    \"content_types\": [\"news\", \"blogs\", \"reviews\", \"social\"]\r\n                }\r\n            )\r\n            \r\n            # Process and categorize mentions\r\n            processed_mentions = []\r\n            for mention in mentions:\r\n                processed_mention = {\r\n                    \'url\': mention[\'url\'],\r\n                    \'title\': mention[\'title\'],\r\n                    \'snippet\': mention[\'snippet\'],\r\n                    \'source_type\': self.categorize_source(mention[\'url\']),\r\n                    \'sentiment\': await self.analyze_sentiment(mention[\'snippet\']),\r\n                    \'location_relevance\': self.calculate_location_relevance(mention, location),\r\n                    \'timestamp\': mention.get(\'timestamp\'),\r\n                    \'domain_authority\': await self.get_domain_authority(mention[\'url\'])\r\n                }\r\n                processed_mentions.append(processed_mention)\r\n            \r\n            location_data[location[\'name\']] = {\r\n                \'total_mentions\': len(processed_mentions),\r\n                \'mentions\': processed_mentions,\r\n                \'sentiment_breakdown\': self.calculate_sentiment_breakdown(processed_mentions),\r\n                \'top_sources\': self.get_top_sources(processed_mentions),\r\n                \'trending_topics\': self.extract_trending_topics(processed_mentions)\r\n            }\r\n        \r\n        return location_data\r\n    \r\n    def build_geographic_query(self, brand_name, location):\r\n        \"\"\"Build location-specific search query\"\"\"\r\n        location_terms = [\r\n            location[\'city\'],\r\n            location.get(\'state\', \'\'),\r\n            location.get(\'neighborhood\', \'\'),\r\n            location.get(\'zip_code\', \'\')\r\n        ]\r\n        \r\n        # Filter out empty terms\r\n        location_terms = [term for term in location_terms if term]\r\n        \r\n        return f\'\"{brand_name}\" {\" OR \".join(location_terms)}\'\r\n    \r\n    def categorize_source(self, url):\r\n        \"\"\"Categorize the source type\"\"\"\r\n        domain = url.split(\'/\')[2].lower()\r\n        \r\n        if any(review_site in domain for review_site in [\'yelp\', \'google\', \'tripadvisor\', \'foursquare\']):\r\n            return \'review\'\r\n        elif any(news_site in domain for news_site in [\'news\', \'tribune\', \'times\', \'post\', \'herald\']):\r\n            return \'news\'\r\n        elif any(social_site in domain for social_site in [\'facebook\', \'twitter\', \'instagram\', \'linkedin\']):\r\n            return \'social\'\r\n        elif \'blog\' in domain or any(blog_platform in domain for blog_platform in [\'wordpress\', \'medium\', \'substack\']):\r\n            return \'blog\'\r\n        else:\r\n            return \'other\'\r\n```\r\n\r\n**UI Components**:\r\n- Multi-location dashboard with map visualization\r\n- Location-specific mention feeds\r\n- Sentiment tracking by geography\r\n- Source type breakdown by location\r\n- Alert configuration per location\r\n\r\n### 2. Local Competitor Intelligence\r\n**User Story**: \"As a regional manager, I want to track what my competitors are doing in each of my markets, so I can adjust local strategy accordingly.\"\r\n\r\n**Technical Implementation**:\r\n```python\r\nclass LocalCompetitorMonitor:\r\n    def __init__(self, perplexity_client):\r\n        self.perplexity = perplexity_client\r\n    \r\n    async def track_local_competitors(self, competitors, locations, business_category):\r\n        \"\"\"Track competitor activities across geographic markets\"\"\"\r\n        competitor_intelligence = {}\r\n        \r\n        for location in locations:\r\n            competitor_intelligence[location[\'name\']] = {}\r\n            \r\n            for competitor in competitors:\r\n                # Search for competitor activities in specific location\r\n                competitor_query = f\'\"{competitor}\" {location[\"city\"]} {business_category}\'\r\n                \r\n                activities = await self.perplexity.search(\r\n                    query=competitor_query,\r\n                    filters={\r\n                        \"geographic_scope\": location[\'geo_filter\'],\r\n                        \"time_range\": \"last_30_days\",\r\n                        \"domains\": [\"exclude_spam_domains\"]\r\n                    }\r\n                )\r\n                \r\n                # Analyze competitor activities\r\n                activity_analysis = {\r\n                    \'new_locations\': self.detect_new_locations(activities, competitor),\r\n                    \'promotional_activities\': self.detect_promotions(activities),\r\n                    \'media_coverage\': self.detect_media_mentions(activities),\r\n                    \'review_trends\': await self.analyze_review_trends(activities, competitor),\r\n                    \'local_partnerships\': self.detect_partnerships(activities),\r\n                    \'activity_score\': self.calculate_activity_score(activities)\r\n                }\r\n                \r\n                competitor_intelligence[location[\'name\']][competitor] = activity_analysis\r\n        \r\n        return competitor_intelligence\r\n    \r\n    def detect_new_locations(self, activities, competitor):\r\n        \"\"\"Detect if competitor opened new locations\"\"\"\r\n        new_location_keywords = [\r\n            \'new location\', \'grand opening\', \'now open\', \r\n            \'opening soon\', \'expanded to\', \'new store\'\r\n        ]\r\n        \r\n        new_locations = []\r\n        for activity in activities:\r\n            if any(keyword in activity[\'snippet\'].lower() for keyword in new_location_keywords):\r\n                new_locations.append({\r\n                    \'announcement\': activity[\'snippet\'],\r\n                    \'source\': activity[\'url\'],\r\n                    \'date\': activity.get(\'timestamp\')\r\n                })\r\n        \r\n        return new_locations\r\n    \r\n    def detect_promotions(self, activities):\r\n        \"\"\"Detect promotional activities\"\"\"\r\n        promo_keywords = [\r\n            \'sale\', \'discount\', \'promotion\', \'special offer\',\r\n            \'limited time\', \'deal\', \'coupon\', \'free\'\r\n        ]\r\n        \r\n        promotions = []\r\n        for activity in activities:\r\n            if any(keyword in activity[\'snippet\'].lower() for keyword in promo_keywords):\r\n                promotions.append({\r\n                    \'promotion_text\': activity[\'snippet\'],\r\n                    \'source\': activity[\'url\'],\r\n                    \'detected_date\': activity.get(\'timestamp\')\r\n                })\r\n        \r\n        return promotions\r\n```\r\n\r\n### 3. Local Search Performance Tracking\r\n**User Story**: \"As a franchise marketing director, I want to see how each location performs in local search results and AI recommendations.\"\r\n\r\n**Technical Implementation**:\r\n```python\r\nclass LocalSearchTracker:\r\n    def __init__(self, perplexity_client):\r\n        self.perplexity = perplexity_client\r\n        self.local_search_queries = [\r\n            \"{category} near me\",\r\n            \"best {category} in {city}\",\r\n            \"{category} {city}\",\r\n            \"top rated {category} {city}\"\r\n        ]\r\n    \r\n    async def track_local_search_performance(self, business_info, locations):\r\n        \"\"\"Track how business appears in local search across locations\"\"\"\r\n        performance_data = {}\r\n        \r\n        for location in locations:\r\n            location_performance = {\r\n                \'traditional_search\': {},\r\n                \'ai_recommendations\': {},\r\n                \'local_pack_presence\': {},\r\n                \'review_visibility\': {}\r\n            }\r\n            \r\n            for query_template in self.local_search_queries:\r\n                # Build location-specific query\r\n                query = query_template.format(\r\n                    category=business_info[\'category\'],\r\n                    city=location[\'city\']\r\n                )\r\n                \r\n                # Traditional SERP tracking\r\n                serp_results = await self.get_local_serp_results(query, location)\r\n                position = self.find_business_position(serp_results, business_info[\'name\'])\r\n                \r\n                # AI platform recommendations\r\n                ai_recommendations = await self.check_ai_recommendations(query, business_info[\'name\'])\r\n                \r\n                location_performance[\'traditional_search\'][query] = {\r\n                    \'position\': position,\r\n                    \'local_pack_position\': self.find_local_pack_position(serp_results, business_info[\'name\']),\r\n                    \'featured_in_map\': self.check_map_presence(serp_results, business_info[\'name\'])\r\n                }\r\n                \r\n                location_performance[\'ai_recommendations\'][query] = ai_recommendations\r\n            \r\n            performance_data[location[\'name\']] = location_performance\r\n        \r\n        return performance_data\r\n    \r\n    async def check_ai_recommendations(self, query, business_name):\r\n        \"\"\"Check if business is recommended by AI platforms\"\"\"\r\n        ai_response = await self.perplexity.chat.completions.create(\r\n            model=\"sonar-pro\",\r\n            messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": query}]\r\n        )\r\n        \r\n        response_text = ai_response.choices[0].message.content\r\n        citations = getattr(ai_response.choices[0].message, \'citations\', [])\r\n        \r\n        return {\r\n            \'mentioned\': business_name.lower() in response_text.lower(),\r\n            \'recommendation_context\': self.extract_mention_context(response_text, business_name),\r\n            \'citation_included\': any(business_name.lower() in citation.get(\'url\', \'\').lower() for citation in citations),\r\n            \'recommendation_strength\': self.assess_recommendation_strength(response_text, business_name)\r\n        }\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## User Experience Flow\r\n\r\n### 1. Quick Setup (5 minutes)\r\n1. Enter business name and category\r\n2. Add locations (city, state, radius)\r\n3. Add 2-3 main competitors\r\n4. Set monitoring frequency\r\n5. Configure alert preferences\r\n\r\n### 2. Daily Dashboard Review\r\n1. Location performance overview map\r\n2. New mentions by location\r\n3. Competitor activity alerts\r\n4. Local search ranking changes\r\n5. Review sentiment trends\r\n\r\n### 3. Location-Specific Deep Dive\r\n1. Select location from map/list\r\n2. View mention feed for that location\r\n3. Analyze competitor activities\r\n4. Check local search performance\r\n5. Export location-specific report\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Technical Architecture\r\n\r\n### Backend Implementation\r\n```python\r\n# FastAPI with geographic data optimization\r\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\r\nfrom geopy.geocoders import Nominatim\r\nimport geoip2.database\r\n\r\napp = FastAPI()\r\n\r\nclass LocationManager:\r\n    def __init__(self):\r\n        self.geocoder = Nominatim(user_agent=\"localiq_monitor\")\r\n        self.geoip_reader = geoip2.database.Reader(\'GeoIP2-City.mmdb\')\r\n    \r\n    def geocode_location(self, location_string):\r\n        \"\"\"Convert location string to geographic coordinates\"\"\"\r\n        try:\r\n            location = self.geocoder.geocode(location_string)\r\n            return {\r\n                \'latitude\': location.latitude,\r\n                \'longitude\': location.longitude,\r\n                \'formatted_address\': location.address\r\n            }\r\n        except:\r\n            return None\r\n    \r\n    def create_geo_filter(self, location, radius_miles=25):\r\n        \"\"\"Create geographic filter for Perplexity API\"\"\"\r\n        coords = self.geocode_location(f\"{location[\'city\']}, {location[\'state\']}\")\r\n        if coords:\r\n            return {\r\n                \'center_lat\': coords[\'latitude\'],\r\n                \'center_lng\': coords[\'longitude\'],\r\n                \'radius_miles\': radius_miles,\r\n                \'geo_string\': f\"{location[\'city\']}, {location[\'state\']}\"\r\n            }\r\n        return None\r\n\r\n# Database Models\r\nclass LocationMonitor(Base):\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    user_id = Column(String, index=True)\r\n    business_name = Column(String)\r\n    location_name = Column(String)\r\n    city = Column(String)\r\n    state = Column(String)\r\n    latitude = Column(Float)\r\n    longitude = Column(Float)\r\n    radius_miles = Column(Integer, default=25)\r\n    created_at = Column(DateTime)\r\n\r\nclass LocationMention(Base):\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    location_monitor_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\'locationmonitors.id\'))\r\n    url = Column(String)\r\n    title = Column(String)\r\n    snippet = Column(Text)\r\n    source_type = Column(String)  # news, review, blog, social\r\n    sentiment = Column(String)    # positive, negative, neutral\r\n    relevance_score = Column(Float)\r\n    detected_at = Column(DateTime)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Frontend Components\r\n```javascript\r\n// Location-centric dashboard\r\nimport { MapContainer, TileLayer, Marker, Popup } from \'react-leaflet\'\r\n\r\nexport function LocalIQDashboard({ userId }) {\r\n    const [selectedLocation, setSelectedLocation] = useState(null)\r\n    const [locations, setLocations] = useState([])\r\n    const [mentionData, setMentionData] = useState({})\r\n    \r\n    const { data: locationMentions } = useQuery(\r\n        [\'location-mentions\', userId, selectedLocation],\r\n        () => fetchLocationMentions(userId, selectedLocation)\r\n    )\r\n    \r\n    return (\r\n        <div className=\"grid grid-cols-12 gap-6\">\r\n            <div className=\"col-span-8\">\r\n                <MapContainer center={[39.8283, -98.5795]} zoom={4} className=\"h-96\">\r\n                    <TileLayer url=\"https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png\" />\r\n                    {locations.map(location => (\r\n                        <Marker \r\n                            key={location.id}\r\n                            position={[location.latitude, location.longitude]}\r\n                            eventHandlers={{\r\n                                click: () => setSelectedLocation(location.id)\r\n                            }}\r\n                        >\r\n                            <Popup>\r\n                                <div>\r\n                                    <h3>{location.name}</h3>\r\n                                    <p>Mentions: {mentionData[location.id]?.total || 0}</p>\r\n                                    <p>Sentiment: {mentionData[location.id]?.sentiment || \'N/A\'}</p>\r\n                                </div>\r\n                            </Popup>\r\n                        </Marker>\r\n                    ))}\r\n                </MapContainer>\r\n            </div>\r\n            \r\n            <div className=\"col-span-4\">\r\n                <LocationPerformanceCard location={selectedLocation} />\r\n                <CompetitorActivityFeed location={selectedLocation} />\r\n            </div>\r\n            \r\n            <div className=\"col-span-12\">\r\n                <LocationMentionsTable mentions={locationMentions} />\r\n            </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n    )\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Development Timeline: 5 Days\r\n\r\n### Day 1: Geographic Infrastructure\r\n- [ ] Set up location geocoding system\r\n- [ ] Implement geographic filtering for Perplexity API\r\n- [ ] Create location management database models\r\n- [ ] Build location setup interface\r\n\r\n### Day 2: Brand Monitoring Engine\r\n- [ ] Implement geographic brand mention tracking\r\n- [ ] Build sentiment analysis pipeline\r\n- [ ] Create mention categorization system\r\n- [ ] Add source type detection\r\n\r\n### Day 3: Competitor Intelligence\r\n- [ ] Build local competitor monitoring\r\n- [ ] Implement activity detection algorithms\r\n- [ ] Create competitor comparison views\r\n- [ ] Add promotional activity detection\r\n\r\n### Day 4: Search Performance Tracking\r\n- [ ] Implement local search position tracking\r\n- [ ] Build AI recommendation monitoring\r\n- [ ] Create performance visualization\r\n- [ ] Add ranking change alerts\r\n\r\n### Day 5: Dashboard & Polish\r\n- [ ] Complete map-based dashboard\r\n- [ ] Implement location switching\r\n- [ ] Add export functionality\r\n- [ ] Deploy and test\r\n\r\n### Tools Strategy\r\n1. **Claude Code**: Geographic algorithms, API integrations, data processing\r\n2. **Cursor**: Map components, dashboard UI, location management\r\n3. **VS Code**: Database operations, background tasks, testing\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Pricing & Business Model\r\n\r\n### Pricing Structure (Per Location)\r\n1. **Local** ($49/month per location):\r\n   - Basic brand monitoring\r\n   - 3 competitors tracked\r\n   - Weekly reports\r\n   - Email alerts\r\n\r\n2. **Regional** ($99/month per location):\r\n   - Advanced competitor intelligence\r\n   - Daily monitoring\r\n   - Local search tracking\r\n   - Sentiment analysis\r\n   - Custom reporting\r\n\r\n3. **Enterprise** ($149/month per location):\r\n   - Real-time monitoring\r\n   - Unlimited competitors\r\n   - AI recommendation tracking\r\n   - API access\r\n   - White-label reports\r\n\r\n### Revenue Model\r\n- **Franchise Chains**: 20+ locations × $99 = $1,980/month per client\r\n- **Multi-location Retail**: 5-15 locations × $99 = $495-1,485/month\r\n- **Service Networks**: 10+ locations × $149 = $1,490+/month\r\n\r\n### Success Metrics\r\n- Location setup completion rate > 80%\r\n- Average locations per client > 3\r\n- Monthly retention > 85%\r\n- Expansion rate (adding locations) > 25%\r\n\r\nThis is the fastest build of the three products since it primarily leverages geographic filtering capabilities already built into Perplexity\'s API, making it ideal for a quick launch to validate the local market opportunity.', 'must_have', 'pending', 70, '2025-09-26 01:55:24', '2025-09-26 01:55:24');
