(156, 12, 'What is the primary goal of Agile methodology?', 'multiple_choice', 'The primary goal of Agile methodology is to deliver incremental and iterative improvements, allowing teams to adapt to changes quickly.', NULL, 1.00, 1, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:05', '2025-07-31 19:54:05'),
(157, 12, 'Which of the following best describes the Agile approach to project management?', 'multiple_choice', 'Agile is characterized by its flexible and collaborative framework, which encourages team communication and adaptability.', NULL, 1.00, 2, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:05', '2025-07-31 19:54:05'),
(158, 12, 'In Agile methodology, which role is primarily responsible for maximizing the value of the product?', 'multiple_choice', 'The Product Owner is responsible for maximizing the value of the product by prioritizing features and ensuring that the team focuses on delivering the most important work.', NULL, 1.00, 3, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:05', '2025-07-31 19:54:05'),
(159, 12, 'What is a key characteristic of Agile teams?', 'multiple_choice', 'Agile teams are self-organizing and cross-functional, meaning they collaborate across different roles to deliver solutions effectively.', NULL, 1.00, 4, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:05', '2025-07-31 19:54:05'),
(160, 12, 'What is the typical duration of a Sprint in Agile development?', 'multiple_choice', 'A Sprint typically lasts for two weeks, allowing teams to deliver incremental improvements regularly.', NULL, 1.00, 5, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:05', '2025-07-31 19:54:05'),
(161, 12, 'Which Agile framework emphasizes the use of time-boxed iterations?', 'multiple_choice', 'Scrum emphasizes the use of time-boxed iterations, known as Sprints, to facilitate regular delivery and feedback.', NULL, 1.00, 6, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:05', '2025-07-31 19:54:05'),
(162, 12, 'What is the purpose of a Sprint Review?', 'multiple_choice', 'The Sprint Review is intended to demonstrate completed work and gather feedback from stakeholders to inform future development.', NULL, 1.00, 7, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:05', '2025-07-31 19:54:05'),
(163, 12, 'In Agile, what does the term \"backlog\" refer to?', 'multiple_choice', 'The backlog refers to a collection of work items prioritized for future development, guiding the team\'s focus during Sprints.', NULL, 1.00, 8, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:05', '2025-07-31 19:54:05'),
(164, 12, 'Which Agile practice involves daily team meetings to discuss progress and challenges?', 'multiple_choice', 'The Daily Stand-up is a practice where team members meet daily to discuss progress, challenges, and plans for the day.', NULL, 1.00, 9, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:05', '2025-07-31 19:54:05'),
(165, 12, 'What is one major advantage of Agile over traditional project management methods?', 'multiple_choice', 'One major advantage of Agile is its ability to allow for rapid responses to changing requirements, making it adaptable to project needs.', NULL, 1.00, 10, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:05', '2025-07-31 19:54:05'),
(166, 12, 'What is the role of the Scrum Master in Agile?', 'multiple_choice', 'The Scrum Master facilitates and supports the Scrum process, helping the team to overcome obstacles and improve their practices.', NULL, 1.00, 11, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:05', '2025-07-31 19:54:05'),
(167, 12, 'What is the significance of the Agile Manifesto?', 'multiple_choice', 'The Agile Manifesto outlines the values and principles of Agile development, guiding teams in their practices and decision-making.', NULL, 1.00, 12, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:05', '2025-07-31 19:54:05'),
(168, 12, 'Which of the following is NOT considered a principle of Agile?', 'multiple_choice', 'Comprehensive documentation is not considered a principle of Agile; instead, Agile emphasizes working software as a priority.', NULL, 1.00, 13, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:05', '2025-07-31 19:54:05'),
(169, 12, 'How does Agile methodology typically handle changes in project requirements?', 'multiple_choice', 'Agile methodology embraces changes in project requirements, allowing teams to incorporate feedback and adapt as needed throughout the development process.', NULL, 1.00, 14, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:05', '2025-07-31 19:54:05'),
(170, 12, 'What is the main focus during the Retrospective meeting in Agile?', 'multiple_choice', 'The main focus of the Retrospective meeting is on reviewing and improving team processes and performance to enhance efficiency and outcomes in future Sprints.', NULL, 1.00, 15, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:05', '2025-07-31 19:54:05'),
(171, 13, 'Which of the following project management methodologies is characterized by a linear and sequential approach?', 'multiple_choice', 'The Waterfall methodology follows a linear and sequential process, where each phase must be completed before the next begins.', NULL, 1.00, 1, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:37', '2025-07-31 19:54:37'),
(172, 13, 'In which project management approach is flexibility and adaptability to change emphasized?', 'multiple_choice', 'The Agile approach prioritizes flexibility and adaptability, allowing teams to respond to changes throughout the project lifecycle.', NULL, 1.00, 2, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:37', '2025-07-31 19:54:37'),
(173, 13, 'What is a defining feature of a Hybrid project management approach?', 'multiple_choice', 'The Hybrid approach combines elements from both Waterfall and Agile methodologies to leverage the strengths of each.', NULL, 1.00, 3, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:37', '2025-07-31 19:54:37'),
(174, 13, 'Which of the following is NOT a characteristic of the Waterfall model?', 'multiple_choice', 'The Waterfall model does not involve frequent iterations; it progresses through distinct phases without revisiting previous ones.', NULL, 1.00, 4, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:37', '2025-07-31 19:54:37'),
(175, 13, 'Which Agile framework is commonly used to manage software development projects?', 'multiple_choice', 'Kanban is an Agile framework that helps teams manage and visualize their work in progress, commonly applied in software development.', NULL, 1.00, 5, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:37', '2025-07-31 19:54:37'),
(176, 13, 'What is the primary benefit of using Agile methods in project management?', 'multiple_choice', 'Agile methods prioritize collaboration with customers, ensuring their feedback is incorporated throughout the project.', NULL, 1.00, 6, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:37', '2025-07-31 19:54:37'),
(177, 13, 'In a Waterfall project, when is the testing phase typically conducted?', 'multiple_choice', 'In the Waterfall model, the testing phase occurs after the development phase has been completed.', NULL, 1.00, 7, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:37', '2025-07-31 19:54:37'),
(178, 13, 'Which of the following best describes the term \"sprint\" in Agile methodology?', 'multiple_choice', 'A \"sprint\" in Agile is a short, time-boxed period during which specific tasks or features are completed.', NULL, 1.00, 8, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:37', '2025-07-31 19:54:37'),
(179, 13, 'What is a primary challenge associated with the Waterfall methodology?', 'multiple_choice', 'A primary challenge of the Waterfall model is that it is difficult to manage changes once the project has moved past the initial requirements phase.', NULL, 1.00, 9, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:37', '2025-07-31 19:54:37'),
(180, 13, 'Which project management approach is most likely to use iterative cycles for development and testing?', 'multiple_choice', 'Agile methodologies utilize iterative cycles, allowing for continuous development and testing throughout the project.', NULL, 1.00, 10, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:37', '2025-07-31 19:54:37'),
(181, 13, 'What is a common method used in Agile practices to track progress?', 'multiple_choice', 'A Burn-down Chart is commonly used in Agile practices to track progress against the amount of work remaining.', NULL, 1.00, 11, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:37', '2025-07-31 19:54:37'),
(182, 13, 'Which of the following roles is typically found in an Agile team?', 'multiple_choice', 'The Scrum Master is a key role in Agile teams, responsible for facilitating the Scrum process and supporting the team.', NULL, 1.00, 12, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:37', '2025-07-31 19:54:37'),
(183, 13, 'In the context of project management approaches, which of the following statements is true?', 'multiple_choice', 'Hybrid approaches allow for adaptation to different project needs by combining elements from both Waterfall and Agile methodologies.', NULL, 1.00, 13, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:37', '2025-07-31 19:54:37'),
(184, 13, 'Which statement best describes the Agile principle of customer collaboration?', 'multiple_choice', 'The Agile principle emphasizes ongoing customer collaboration and feedback throughout the project to ensure the final product meets their needs.', NULL, 1.00, 14, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:37', '2025-07-31 19:54:37'),
(185, 13, 'In what scenario would a project manager likely choose a Hybrid approach?', 'multiple_choice', 'A Hybrid approach is suitable when both a fixed timeline and budget are critical, while still allowing for some degree of flexibility.', NULL, 1.00, 15, 1, NULL, NULL, '2025-07-31 19:54:37', '2025-07-31 19:54:37'),
